Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Cash flow from operating activities grew by more than 11.7% from Year 1 to Year 2.', 'A business can have a negative cash flow from investing activities in the same year that it pays a dividend, since investment spending and dividends sit in different sections of the cash flow statement.', 'Customer collections of receivables are classified as financing cash inflows.', 'After depreciation, the carrying value of an asset on the balance sheet is lower than its original cost.', 'Cost of sales includes administration costs, shipping to customers and sales-staff costs.'], ARRAY[false, true, false, true, false], ARRAY['FALSE — Use the case figures for Cash flow from operating activities and compute the percentage change between Year 1 and Year 2 before comparing it with the claimed threshold.

