Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Return on capital employed, the operating result taken relative to equity plus non-current liabilities, exceeds 25.8%.', 'The equity ratio exceeds 47.3%.', 'Cash flow from operating activities amounts to less than 82.1% of the operating result, indicating profit is only partly backed by cash.', 'Non-current assets normally have a useful life of more than one year and are intended to be used in the business for longer than one year.', 'Return on equity, the operating result taken as a percentage of total equity, exceeds 24.6%.'], ARRAY[false, false, false, true, true], ARRAY['FALSE — ROCE relates operating result to capital employed: equity plus non-current liabilities.

Name the identity in words: ROCE = operating result ÷ (equity + non-current liabilities).

$$
\text{Capital employed} = 543 + 417 + 44 = 1,004
$$

$$
ROCE = \frac{227}{1,004} = 22.6\%
$$

Threshold: exceeds 25.8%. Actual 22.6%.

Reading the arithmetic against the claim: ROCE 22.6% does not exceed 25.8% so the statement does not hold.

The statement is false.', 'FALSE — The equity ratio places equity against total assets so the financing structure can be judged on one balance sheet.

