$$

$$
\frac{57 - 42}{42} = 35.7\%
$$

Threshold: more than 36.2%. Actual 35.7%.

Reading the arithmetic against the claim: the gap is 35.7%, which does not exceed 36.2% so the statement does not hold.

The statement is false.'], '4/5', 90, 'full' ),
